          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "quercus is inherited, probably from Proto-Italic kwerkus, \"oak\" (EtymDB 2.1). It is usually traced to Proto-Indo-European perkwus, \"oak\", with the first sound changed to match the second, as in coquō, \"to cook\". English fir is a distant cousin."
